id: intl/numbers-and-text/compact/0001
area: intl
op: Intl.NumberFormat.prototype.format
in: str:"en" str:"short" f64:0x408F3C0000000000
out: value: str:"1K"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: rows N6a and N6f: Compact's exponent after rounding: 999.5, 999.995, 999999 in `en`, `de`, short and long; Broiler.JS answers `"1000"`, `"1000"`, `"1000K"`; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0082, C1) | Compact's magnitude by `Math.Log10` and `Math.Pow`: 999999.9999999999, 1e21-1e24, engineering, `en` and `de`; Broiler.JS answers `"1000K"`, `"1000 thousand"`, `de` `"1.000.000"`; 1e21-1e24 alike; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0082, C1); answered by SJL-9.5, this engine's cut-over to the shared Intl library
prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-computeexponent spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-getnotationsubpattern ref:intlref@1
script: new Intl.NumberFormat("en", {notation: "compact", compactDisplay: "short"}).format($f64(0x408f3c00, 0x00000000))
note: rows N6a and N6f: ComputeExponent's exponent after rounding, over the exact value
since: 27

