prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-chainnumberformat ref:intlref@1
script: (function () { var o = Object.create(Intl.NumberFormat.prototype); var r = Intl.NumberFormat.call(o, "de"); return [r === o, Intl.NumberFormat.prototype.resolvedOptions.call(r).locale].join(); })()
note: row N12 (implementation-defined): the normative-optional legacy constructor mode, which each engine keeps; ChainNumberFormat is normative optional; Broiler.VM implements it, so the call answers its receiver, and Broiler.JS does not, so the call answers a new NumberFormat; JSD-0082 keeps each engine's choice (rows N12 and T5)
