note: rows N14 (data, C5) and N1b (data, C5): the shared data's de-CH, not the host's culture; decision D5: Broiler.VM's locale list stays de, de-DE, en and en-US, so it resolves de-CH to de (LookupMatcher over its list, rows L28 and T16) and its expectation is the reference's answer for that locale; Broiler.JS's embedding carries the locale, so its expectation is out
