id: intl/numbers-and-text/relative/0040
area: intl
op: Intl.RelativeTimeFormat.prototype.format
in: str:"en" f64:0x4028000000000000
out: value: str:"in \u0661\u0662 days"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row S5: The `numberingSystem` option: `en` `arab` `format(12, "day")` and `formatToParts`, `de` `thai`; `en-u-nu-arab`; Broiler.JS answers `"in 12 days"`, `"vor 1.234,5 Tagen"`: the inner NumberFormat is built without the option; `en-u-nu-arab` works; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0082, C1); answered by SJL-9.5, this engine's cut-over to the shared Intl library
prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-Intl.RelativeTimeFormat ref:intlref@1
script: new Intl.RelativeTimeFormat("en", {numberingSystem: "arab"}).format(12, "day")
note: row S5: the numberingSystem reaches the inner NumberFormat
since: 27

