op: Intl.ListFormat.prototype.format
in: str:"no"
out: value: str:"A, B og C"
class: impl-defined
per-engine.broiler-js: value: str:"A, B og C"
per-engine.broiler-vm: value: str:"A, B, and C"
divergence.broiler-js: row S1b: Other locales: `es`, `fr`, `it`, `ja`, `zh`, `pl`, `ru`, `ar`, `he`, `xyz`; Broiler.JS answers the package's: `es` `"A, B, C y D"`, `ja` `"AU+3001BU+3001CU+3001D"`; `he` resolves `he` with English patterns `"A and B"` ...; data policy (C5): its embedding takes CLDR 48.2.0 for every locale of decision D5's list; answered by SJL-9.5, this engine's cut-over to the shared Intl library
prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-formatlist ref:intlref@1
script: new Intl.ListFormat("no").format(["A", "B", "C"])
note: row S1b (data, C5): list patterns; no, one of Broiler.JS's extra locales (decision D5): the table family's CLDR data; decision D5: Broiler.VM's locale list stays de, de-DE, en and en-US, so it resolves no to en-US (LookupMatcher over its list, rows L28 and T16) and its expectation is the reference's answer for that locale; Broiler.JS's embedding carries the locale, so its expectation is out
since: 27

